KNOWNBUG (empty pack expansion in a call): [temp.variadic]/5 -- expanding an
empty parameter pack in a function-call argument list yields an empty argument
list, so `base(a...)` with zero pack elements is the call `base()`.  CBMC
instead reports "found no match for symbol 'base'".  Part of the unified
pack-expansion rework documented in
doc/architectural/cpp-variadic-pack-expansion-rework.md.  Reclassify CORE once
an empty pack expansion produces an empty argument list.
